{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["מקום לנו ללין — a place for us in your house, and whatever else we need." "ללין — it is a noun, 'a lodging house,' as in ״כי יהיה ריב בין אנשים״, from וירב בלבן; בין דין לדין — [a noun] from וילן שם בלילה it is. But she said: גם מקום ללון — its meaning is 'for you yourselves to lodge,' like לקום לשוב מצרימה. And had she said גם מקום לכם as they said מקום לנו, she should have said ללין as they said — which would have meant 'also a place for you'; and why? A lodging house. But ללון needs no explanation, for it naturally means 'to lodge in it' — people [lodging]. This is the essential plain sense for one who scrutinizes the language of Holy Scripture."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "The comment contains a sequence of grammatical illustrations (rib, lavan, din) whose connective syntax in the Hebrew is compressed; translated hyper-literally to preserve Rashbam's chain of examples without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:00.996134296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}